 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "sessions is a list of strings \"<user_id>,<input_tokens>,<output_tokens>,<plan>\" with canonical decimal token counts. pricing is a list of comma-separated plan rows; every plan used by a session has exactly one row. Prices are non-negative integers in an abstract smallest currency unit per token, so every amount is an exact integer. Return [user_id, total] for every user that has at least one session, sorted by user_id in code-point order. Level 1: a pricing row is \"<plan>,<input_price>,<output_price>\". A session costs input_tokens * input_price + output_tokens * output_price, and a user's total is the sum over their sessions.",
